WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.330
MALIK GEORGE: What's going on?

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:04.780
I'm Malik.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.370
MILES GEORGE: I'm Miles.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.300
We're Malik and Miles.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.830
MALIK GEORGE: And we're
MIT undergraduates.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.570
MILES GEORGE: And we're going to
talk about the top five reasons

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.350
to study the brain.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.490
MALIK GEORGE: Coming in at 5.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.032
MILES GEORGE: You can find the
cure to any biological disease

00:00:14.032 --> 00:00:15.150
that affects the brain.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:15.748
Number four--

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.790
MALIK GEORGE: You can
literally learn the biology

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.380
that governs behavior.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.505
Coming in at three--

00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:23.070
MILES GEORGE: You can understand
the most complex thing

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.840
in the known universe.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.180
MALIK GEORGE:
Besides us, that is.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:27.698
GROUP: Nah.

00:00:27.698 --> 00:00:28.740
MILES GEORGE: Number two.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.698
MALIK GEORGE: Pop quiz.

00:00:29.698 --> 00:00:31.870
What is the only organ
that has named itself?

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:32.370
[BUZZER]

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:32.790
[CROWD CHEERING]

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:33.580
MILES GEORGE: It's the brain.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.770
MALIK GEORGE: And
finally, number one.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.390
MILES GEORGE: And it's
the most important.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.460
Neurons have the coolest
shape of literally any cell.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:38.580
[MARKER SOUNDS]

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.913
Like, a normal cell is like
this, but a neuron is like--

00:00:40.913 --> 00:00:41.550
[MARKER SOUNDS]

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.008
If they're not
animating this, this

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:45.010
is going to look really weird.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.800
MALIK GEORGE: But if
you're not convinced

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.000
this will change your mind.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.590
One, and two, and--

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.560
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.010
We'll see you next time.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:54.760
MILES GEORGE: Bye.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.260
[MUSIC PLAYING]

